# Portfolio-first — `aideazz.xyz/portfolio` leads, the apex supports

`https://aideazz.xyz` is the **vision site**. `https://aideazz.xyz/portfolio` is the
**money page**: the one buyers land on, the one outreach points at, and the one we
want AI assistants to cite. When a choice exists, the portfolio wins.

## Rules

1. **Order lists portfolio-first.** Audit targets, sitemaps, docs tables, nav — the
   portfolio is row one, the apex is row two. Never lead with the apex.
2. **Every artifact links back to the hub.** `/api`, `/blog`, `sop-ai-ops.html`, the
   Atlas board and the podcast each carry a return link to `/portfolio`, so a crawler
   entering on any page can reach the hub in one hop.
3. **Outbound destinations are the portfolio.** Outreach emails, HubSpot notes,
   Telegram lead pings and the `/api` page send people to `/portfolio`, not the apex.
4. **Entity files name the portfolio as primary.** `llms.txt`, its `.well-known`
   mirror and `geo-manifest.json` declare `/portfolio` as the primary entity page;
   the sitemap gives it the highest priority.
5. **Citation tracking scores the portfolio first.** A citation of `/portfolio` is the
   headline number; an apex citation is recorded but reported as secondary.

## The six proof surfaces

The portfolio must link to all of these, and each should link back:

| Surface | URL |
| --- | --- |
| Audit API + free tool | `https://aideazz.xyz/api` |
| Atlas board | `https://webhook.aideazz.xyz/whitespace/atlas.html` |
| Inquiry form | `https://aideazz.xyz/portfolio#portfolio-inquiry-form` |
| Ops & marketing engine SOP | `https://aideazz.xyz/sop-ai-ops.html` |
| Blog | `https://aideazz.xyz/blog` |
| Podcast | `https://podcast.aideazz.xyz/` |

## Why this is not cosmetic

4everland serves one `index.html` for every route, so a route missing from the
aideazz repo's `scripts/prerender-routes.mjs` silently inherits **homepage** identity —
same title, same description, same schema — and still scores A+ in the visibility
audit, because it *is* the A+ homepage. Adding a route to the portfolio's link graph
is only real once that route has its own prerendered identity. Verify with
`node scripts/visibility-self-audit.cjs <url>` and compare titles, never scores alone.
